WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.020
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 5: On the Farm.

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:07.600
In this unit, your child learns about the farm.

3
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:13.400
They name farm animals and the sounds they make,
learn farm words like tractor, barn and field,

4
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.580
and talk about what people do on a
farm — feeding, planting and picking.

5
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:23.300
They meet the idea that animals and plants
grow (a chick from an egg, a bean from a seed),

6
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.720
and they hear a gentle story about helping and hard work.

7
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.360
The goal is warm, confident spoken
English — not perfect spelling.

8
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:38.340
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:45.620
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
farm animals (cow, hen, chick, duck, sheep, goat, horse…).

10
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.160
you will also say the sound each
animal makes (moo, cluck, quack, baa…).

11
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:56.480
you will also name farm places and things
(farm, barn, field, tractor, egg, seed).

12
00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:59.000
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.980
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: cow, hen, chick, duck, goose, pig.

14
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.220
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.640
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:17.900
The reading sequence includes Amal and
the Little Hen and Talk about On the Farm.

17
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.200
Read actively.

18
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.440
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.480
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:32.660
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

21
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:39.040
Listen to the model, point to the matching
picture, then say the pattern: This is a ___.

22
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.680
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.160
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

24
00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.120
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.620
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.140
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.640
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.580
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:13.180
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.900
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
